{"id": "zscore-global-and-variants", "name": "Z-score and related scale normalisers", "family": "latent", "subfamily": "normalization", "plain": "Plain rescales to unit variance, differing in scope, and scope matters most. SV uses a single global mean/std across the batch and channels, so samples bleed into one another. CampB does per sample. Valkymaera offers a list and a per_channel switch (list read, bodies not). JTrigger can keep the mean.", "math": "SV: (x\u2212mean(x))/std(x) global\nLT norm: same; LT mean: x\u2212mean+arg; LT std: x\u00b7arg/std (no centring)\nCampB normalize: per sample, +\u03b5\nJTrigger: (x\u2212\u03bc)\u00b7\u03c3t/\u03c3+\u03bct with per-channel over spatial", "props": {"operates_on": "LATENT", "params": "method; per_channel; strength"}, "evidence": [{"where": "SirVeggie__comfyui-sv-nodes/__init__.py:1673", "symbol": "samples.std"}, {"where": "Machines-of-Disruption__latent-tools/latent_op.py:41", "symbol": "samples.std()"}, {"where": "JTriggerFish__ComfyLatentTools/core/latent_filters.py:90", "symbol": "def normalize_tensor"}, {"where": "valkymaera__ComfyCollectorNodes/nodes/latent_utils.py:109", "symbol": "METHODS"}], "providers": [{"pack": "SirVeggie__comfyui-sv-nodes", "author": "SirVeggie", "licence": "none-found", "kind": "original", "nodes": ["SV-NormalizeSamples"], "note": "", "verdict": "MAYBE", "risks": ["paid or partner API", "patches torch or ComfyUI globally"], "res4lyf": false}, {"pack": "Machines-of-Disruption__latent-tools", "author": "Machines-of-Disruption", "licence": "MIT", "kind": "variant", "nodes": ["LTLatentOp"], "note": "", "verdict": "", "risks": [], "res4lyf": false}, {"pack": "JTriggerFish__ComfyLatentTools", "author": "JTriggerFish", "licence": "Apache-2.0", "kind": "variant", "nodes": [], "note": "", "verdict": "TRY", "risks": [], "res4lyf": false}, {"pack": "valkymaera__ComfyCollectorNodes", "author": "valkymaera", "licence": "MIT", "kind": "variant", "nodes": ["LatentNormalize"], "note": "method bodies not